+# MASTER7 JILI safety release 150
+
+This release hardens the existing JILI transfer-wallet candidate without enabling production game play or money movement.
+
+Verified platform behavior:
+
+- `jili_myr_1to1` and `jili_my1_1to100` retain independent accounts, cache keys, player namespaces and ledger namespaces.
+- Each live read-only catalogue currently returns 297 entries. A catalogue count is not launch, wallet or settlement acceptance.
+- A launch cannot reserve or submit funds unless the exact customer return origin is allowlisted.
+- Every nonzero transfer-submit result stays `unknown` until the original transaction ID is confirmed by query. Recovery never resubmits that money action.
+- Signed report amounts stay fail-closed because the merchant-specific sign convention has not been confirmed.
+
+Production remains closed. JILI must confirm the account-bound legacy contract, transfer/query/balance/report units for both profiles, launch origins, session closure, late-round finality and signed report semantics. Each profile then needs separate launch, wallet, settlement and recovery acceptance evidence.
